\ ff-test: lines
\ Evaluations nested past FF_EVAL_DEPTH.
\
\ Each `evaluate` is a C call of ff_eval() on the host's stack, so a
\ recursion through it used to run until the host's stack overflowed.
\ Past FF_EVAL_DEPTH evaluations the next one raises -5 (return stack
\ overflow): `evaluate` leaves it as its status, the levels above it
\ finish, and the engine carries on.

variable levels  0 levels !
variable status  0 status !
: r  1 levels +!  "r" evaluate ?dup if status ! then ;
r
status @ . cr
levels @ 1 > . cr
1 2 + . cr
